# DevOps agent

- `backend` runs FastAPI on 8000; `web` runs standalone Next.js on 3000 and is exposed on 8080.
- Next.js uses server-only `BACKEND_URL` for API rewrites.
- Browser WebSocket deployments configure `NEXT_PUBLIC_WS_BASE_URL` or provide an equivalent reverse proxy.
- Use multi-stage builds, deterministic lockfiles, non-root runtime users where practical, and health checks.
- Persist PostgreSQL in `postgres_data`; keep uploads and legacy SQLite migration
  sources in `portal_data`. Back up both volumes before risky changes.
- Document every environment variable and never commit `.env` or secrets.
- Keep generated files out of build contexts and Git.

Validate Compose config and build both images after infrastructure changes.
